{
 "name": "Tank cross-section: M1A2 SEP Abrams turret cheek",
 "category": "armor",
 "description": "Slanted cheek (~30 deg) seen from above: 50 mm front plate, ~500 mm cavity of Burlington-type NERA packets (25 mm steel + 10 mm rubber + 6 mm steel, tilted a further 30 deg), two depleted-uranium armour layers (HA package; tungsten stand-in, no sourced DU data) and a 120 mm back plate. Estimates vs long rods: M1A1HA ~800 mm, M1A2 SEP ~940-960 mm. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
